            %p
          %p
          #OnTheInternalDefinitionOfPrincipality.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (on the internal definition of principality)
              Notice that in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivariantPrincipalBundles"}
              we do
              %em not
              explicitly demand that the base space is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
              of the total space by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
              (it defines an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-torsor"} pseudo-torsor
              instead of a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The way the definition is stated, it involves only
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
                  (no
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  functors on the ambient category, such as notably the
                  = succeed "-functors" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+locus"} fixed locus
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "topological+G-space#FixedLociWithResidualWeylGroupAction"} there
              %li
                %p Nevertheless, the expected quotient condition is both implied as well as circumvented, as need be:
                %p
                  Once equivariant local trivializability is imposed
                  %a{:href => "#NotionsOfEquivariantLocalTriviality"} below
                  it follows that the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial"} locally trivial
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      Either the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typical+fiber"} typical fiber
                      is
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi P
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                      is an
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
                      %a{:href => "#EquivariantPrincipality"} above
                      implies that
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                      is the quotient of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi P
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                      by
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi G
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %li
                    %p
                      Or the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typical+fiber"} typical fiber
                      is the
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+space"} empty space
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivariantPrincipalBundles"}
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ×
