                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            \\Gamma \times \varnothing
                            \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                            \\varnothing \times_X \varnothing
                    %p
                      (since both
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                      and
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
                      are isomorphic to the
                      = succeed "):" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+space"} empty space
                    %p
                      %em Empty bundles are principal! (and locally trivial!), in the above sense.
                    %p
                      While this degenerate case is irrelevant for ordinary principal bundles, it is crucial for equivariant principal bundles, since their
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+loci"} fixed loci
                      often have empty total space. In fact, if the action
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                      of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi G
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                      on the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Γ
